(Useful advice has already been posted in this thread, so I focus on
another aspect...)

To restrict your game by simple formulas is the worst that you can do.
You already experienced that; don't ever forget that!

There are two types of advice in this thread; some give strict values
(like AC, HP, XL, DL) or relations between values. Forget all those;
they're only helpful in very specific circumstances and have no value
for an open, unrestricted, "general purpose" game. And as soon as you
encounter any of Nethack's dozens of different situations around the
next corner or on the next level, where the "rule" won't help or even
hurts, your character will be spoiled. All the other detailled advice
posted upthread is quite good and will help you. Tell those two types
of advice apart.

